it's that time of year to turn down the  lights put on a headset and play horror  games until your skin crawls but it's  also a good time to look ahead to the  frightening games yet to come  here's a list of our top 7 horror games  coming out in 2016 perception is a  first-person narrative horror adventure  perception comes from the deep end games  a group of previous Bioshock developers  led by Bill Gardner play as Cassie a  young woman investigating a mansion in  an abandoned estate but what makes it so  interesting is that she's blind she uses  what we might consider echolocation to  see so any sound creates a king giving  these sites the player will have to use  items like pain to create sounds to see  but you're also giving audio cues to  your location and you're being hunted in  a world filled with horror games where  jump scares and creepy masks are used  often perception has us rely on one of  the most frightening things of all the  unknown steam launch is planned for 2016  doom was one of the most influential and  popular video games in the early 90s and  the reboot by its software looks to be  just as fast brutal and gory as expected  it's technically a shooter but by no  means does it not have horror the series  focuses on the exploits of an unnamed  Space Marine opera  under the UAC who fights hordes of  demons and the undead in order to  survive from the dusty landscapes of  Mars to the blood-splattered depths of  Hell you'll be changing out weapons to  take down memorable threats like zombie  man  pinky demons and the Barons of Hell from  the gameplay we've seen it looks like  fast-paced frenetic carnage so far we  only have a release window of q1 or q2  in 2016 PC ps4 and Xbox one dragon is a  first-person psychological survival  horror game set on the north western  coast of Norway in 1923 Ragnar turn  quits development studio red thread  games have stated that it could be  compared to soma meets the vanishing of  Ethan Carter in a story inspired by  north mythology and New England gothic  you follow a dark and harrowing tale of  one man's descent into madness as he  investigates the disappearance of the  inhabitants of a small Norwegian coastal  community it looks like a slow burning  suspense thriller with an environment  that gave me the same chills as  Apocalypse  dragon is currently in development for  PC Mac Linux and next-gen consoles for  next year  Overkill's The Walking Dead is a co-op  first-person shooter with elements of  action role-playing survival horror and  stealth it invites players to explore  the hugely popular Walking Dead universe  while they'll play the role of a  survivor fending for themselves and a  post-apocalyptic world dominated by  flesh-eating walkers the game is in  development from the studio behind  payday the heist and will include  cooperative online gameplay and be paid  a esque according to The Walking Dead  creator Robert Kirkman the developers  are also working on a VR experience for  the game which will certainly seal the  deal on this frightening experience The  Walking Dead is planned for PC Xbox one  and ps4 last year we were treated to  outlast a surprising or game that really  pushed climatic tension and then aside  psychopaths and crazy experiments that  are gonna kill your the developers was  smart and got right to work on outlast 2  which will be a survival horror  experience and it will take place in the  same universe as outlast  but will have different characters in  two different settings Studio founder  Phillipe Marin told IGN that while the  game won't return players to the  pervasive darkness  of its predecessors Asylum setting the  night vision camera mechanic will return  and based off this trailer it's safe to  say there will be a new type of terror  in the night something that feeds off  the weak of creating a dark and twisted  horror that would leave you mad outlast  2 is planned for a fall 2016 release on  ps4 PC and Xbox one Allison Road is an  upcoming first-person survival horror  video game for PC created by British  developer Lilith limited and published  by team17 it's considered to be a  spiritual successor to PT the playable  teaser for the cancelled video game  silent hill's the player awakens in a  British townhouse with no memory as you  explore the house evidence is gathered  from letters and photos suggesting your  family has been a victim of a heinous  crime also you're not alone and as the  clock continues to tick towards 3:00  a.m. something in the house is stalking  you and making you question your sanity  the gameplay is just a small glimpse  into the world that we're afraid to  enter but it seems just too tempting to  ignore  the release date is TBA 2016 routine is  a first person horror exploration game  set on an abandoned moon base to remind  us of our nightmares from alien and  Space Odyssey the title is the debut  product of English indie studio lunar  software the storyline revolves around  the mysterious disappearance of the crew  members of the lunar research station to  uncover the truth players must travel  through the claustrophobic dark  corridors and rooms of the moon base  uncovering its secrets you won't find  first-aid kits because it's just alive  or dead in space and when I mean dead I  mean  kirmada your main tool is a cat  cosmonaut assistance tool just a repair  device that resembles a gun you upgrade  it with floppy disks found around the  base and in some cases you'll have to  use it as a last resort weapon between  being alone with nothing to calm your  never-ending imagination and being  hunted in a floating tube in space all  of your biggest fears are coming to life  routine has been a little quiet lately  but according to the last devlog it's  still deep in development for a hopeful  2016  so that's our list of seven games to  keep you up all night or at least keep  you at bay until next year happy  Halloween and happy gaming  you
 

